 "run": "r3-e01-agent-evolution",
 "purpose": "r3-e01-agent-evolution: studio experiment E01, what an agent is: a chat model, one tool, many tools, the loop, integrated, agents calling agents; each step adds reach",
 "request": {
  "from": "deck@the-ultimate-insider (tui-mail-public mailroom/ruv-sgit/004-infographic-request-agent-evolution-e01.eml)",
  "date": "2026-10-29",
  "text": "One sentence the audience must understand: an agent is a chat model that was given tools, then more tools, then a loop, then our accounts, and each step added reach. The steps, in order: (1) a chat model answering in a box; (2) one tool; (3) many tools; (4) the loop: it acts, looks at the result and acts again until it decides it is done; (5) integrated: accounts, tokens, other systems; (6) today's agentic flows, agents calling agents. Keep the earlier steps visible as the picture grows. No numbers needed; the loop is Anthropic's own definition in Building effective agents. No dates unless each has a public source; otherwise label the timeline a sketch. A build, each step a few seconds; 40 to 60 seconds; reads as a still at the end. No product logos; no claim that any one product is unsafe; nothing that reads as a forecast. An explainer beside it. Two versions welcome."
 },
